# CODEOWNERS
#
# Auto-requests a review from the listed owner(s) when a PR touches matching
# paths. Owners must have write access to the repo. The LAST matching pattern
# wins. See CONTRIBUTING.md for the full PR workflow.
#
# NOTE: code-owner review is not *required* by branch protection today
# (`require_code_owner_reviews` is off). This is a single-maintainer setup, so
# requiring it would block the author from merging their own PRs. This file
# documents ownership and auto-requests review — it does not gate merges yet.
# When collaborators are added, flip on required code-owner review to enforce it.

# Default owner for everything in the repo
*                       @brandonbuttars

# High-blast-radius areas — called out explicitly so ownership is unambiguous
# as the team grows (all @brandonbuttars for now).
/shared/schema.ts       @brandonbuttars   # single source of truth for the data model
/.github/               @brandonbuttars   # CI, governance, branch-protection-facing config
